  "issue": {
    "issue_key": "MER-206",
    "summary": "Concurrent payment retries can charge the same attempt twice",
    "description": "A gateway timeout triggers overlapping retry workers and the ledger records two charges for a single payment attempt.\n\nTribal constraint: Idempotency keys are per attempt because the ledger reconciler groups on that value; retries within an attempt must reuse it, while a new attempt advances the attempt sequence.",
